senses.gloss:
जालक, अम्, n. a net, woven texture, web; mul-
titude, assemblage; a lattice; an eyelet or loophole;
a nest; a collection or bundle of buds, a germ, an
unblown flower; a plantain, the fruit; illusion; pride;
(अस्), m. a window, a lattice, a loop or eyelethole;
N. of a tree; (इका), f. a net (for catching birds &c.);
chain-armour, armour; a spider; a leech; a kind of
cloth or raiment, woollen cloth; plantain; iron; a
widow, (perhaps so called from the net or braid worn
by widows.)
—जालक-मालिन्, ई, इनी, इ, veiled.

जल्पन, अस्, आ, अम्, speaking, saying, talking;
(अम्), n. talking, saying; chattering, prattling,
garrulity.

जालमानि जालमानि, इस्, m. a patronymic;
(अयस्), m. pl., N. of a subdivision of the Trigarta
people.
